  "result": "The refusals are in `acceptInvitation` in `src/server/services/invitation-service.ts`. It looks up the invitation by the hash of the token in the link, then rejects it in this order:\n- **Cancelled:** if `revokedAt` is set, it throws \"That invitation has been revoked\".\n- **Already used:** if `acceptedAt` is set, it throws \"That invitation has already been accepted\".\n- **Too old:** if `expiresAt` is at or before now, it throws \"That invitation has expired\".\n\nThe setting that decides how old is too old is `DEFAULT_EXPIRY_DAYS = 14`, in the same file. `inviteMembers` passes it as `expiresInDays` when it creates each invitation. The repository turns that into a stored `expiresAt` timestamp, and `acceptInvitation` compares against that stored value. No other file defines an expiry length: the invitation repository only does the day-to-timestamp conversion, and the invite schemas don't set `expiresInDays`.\n\nANSWER: src/server/services/invitation-service.ts",
